		<Title>NTokenizers</Title>
		<PackageReleaseNotes>This is a patch release with a list-parsing behavioral change, a CSS fix for embedded usage (ToHtml).

## Markdown list parsing (behavioral change)

List markers now always interrupt a paragraph, matching the CommonMark spec in practice:

- Any ordered list marker may interrupt a paragraph: any start number (not only 1.) starts a list, instead of lazy-continuing the open paragraph (documented deviation, spec example 303).
- Unordered list markers may interrupt a paragraph as well, including a marker without content.
- A list marker line ends a blockquote: the marker interrupts the quoted paragraph, so the quote closes and the list is parsed in the outer scope.
- The redundant in-list relaxation of the paragraph-interruption rule has been removed.
- WouldStartBlockquoteBreakingConstruct now accepts the ')' ordered delimiter in addition to '.'.

## ToHtml CSS fix

The document layout (max-width, margin, padding) moved from the body element to a .markdown-document wrapper div, so the shared CSS no longer constrains embedded or iframe usage. ToHtmlDocument output now includes a .markdown-document wrapper around the content.</PackageReleaseNotes>
